          "type": "turn",
          "question": "If a document refers to the J45 family, is that a code or a category?",
          "answer": "In the ICD-10-CM classification, J45 is a **category**, not a full code. The asthma category is J45 and sits in Chapter 10, diseases of the respiratory system (source: \"Coding asthma: J45 and its severity and exacerbation axes\").\n\nA full asthma code adds more characters. Two independent axes fill them in: severity (for example, mild intermittent or severe persistent, or \"unspecified\") and the state of the disease at that visit (uncomplicated, with acute exacerbation, or with status asthmaticus). Every combination of the two exists as a code (same source).\n\nThe retrieved passages also say that most categories are not valid at three characters. A code must be carried to its full length (source: \"ICD-10-CM code structure and the conventions that govern selection\").\n\nThe passages did not list the individual full codes for each combination, so I can't tell you which exact code applies to any situation. That is a question for a trained medical coder or the official ICD-10-CM tables.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
